---
// The list on a page of its own, so that an entry's address cut back by one step lands
// somewhere (docs/first-version-choices.md, choice 13).
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import ThingList from '../../components/ThingList.astro';
import { data, headline } from '../../lib/data';

const r = data.headline.records;
---

<Base title="The list · Beyond the Window" description="Every thing on the list, with how far the world has got on each one.">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">The list</p>
    <h1>{headline.words}.</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Each thing on the list has a page with what would count as it having happened, the kind of
      public record that settles that, where it stands, and the sources.
    </p>
  </section>
  <section class="below" style="padding-top: 0">
    <p class="intro">
      "Offered today" means that at least one developer of AI models does the thing, provides it,
      or has publicly committed to it, and a dated public record that is still published says so.
      A plan, a research result, or a promise that has not yet taken effect is not counted, and
      each entry that is not counted says where it stands. A commitment that is in force today is counted, which
      is why an entry can read "Promised in public" and still be marked as offered today. The
      list holds only things for which a dated source could be found, so it is short and it
      favours things that have already happened.
    </p>
    <ThingList />
  </section>
  <section class="below" id="beside">
    <div class="shead"><h2>Beside the List</h2><span>{r.beside_the_list} entries, not counted</span></div>
    <p class="intro">
      These entries are kept because they bear on everything on the list. None is counted, and
      each group says why.
    </p>
    <ThingList beside />
  </section>
</Base>
